# Lockdown mode service posture — sever radios and network services.
# NetworkManager controls the physical NICs, so stopping it (plus the
# chain policy drop in lockdown.nft) is what actually cuts the
# machine off. Tor, dnsmasq and NetworkManager are all stopped — a
# degraded/partial tunnel in lockdown contradicts the mode's "no outbound"
# promise.
# nftables must NOT be toggled: its ExecStop runs `nft flush ruleset`,
# which would silently remove the lockdown kill-switch table the daemon
# loaded right before this step.
- NetworkManager
- tor@default
- dnsmasq